When `GLOO_HAVE_TRANSPORT_IBVERBS` is defined (gloo built with ibverbs, as enabled by `USE_IBVERBS=1`)
`getCvarString` & `getCvarInt` are used for which `Utils.hpp` needs to be included, otherwise:
> GlooDeviceFactory.cpp:158:15: error: 'getCvarString' was not declared in this scope

From https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/182800

diff --git a/torch/csrc/distributed/c10d/GlooDeviceFactory.cpp b/torch/csrc/distributed/c10d/GlooDeviceFactory.cpp
index aefb79cfa3932..45db1faaacd73 100644
--- a/torch/csrc/distributed/c10d/GlooDeviceFactory.cpp
+++ b/torch/csrc/distributed/c10d/GlooDeviceFactory.cpp
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@
 
 #if GLOO_HAVE_TRANSPORT_IBVERBS
 #include <gloo/transport/ibverbs/device.h>
+#include <torch/csrc/distributed/c10d/Utils.hpp>
 #endif
 
 // On Linux, check that the tcp transport is available.
